From dcf2ff2bc7b0c34134b74ca63c2a8ba45b73a229 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 21:44:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] mm: backport file folio fault optimizations

Backport mainline file folio fault optimizations for executable mappings.

Map file-backed large folios in finish_fault() and filemap_map_pages()
when it is safe to do so.

Preserve SIGBUS semantics at i_size boundaries and keep the historical
shmem/tmpfs exception.

Also carry filemap_map_pages() folio reference count optimization and
avoid perturbing mmap_miss when racing on a locked folio.

Use mainline-style file_ra_state order field so VM_EXEC mmap readahead
can request the architecture preferred executable folio order.

On arm64, request 64KB executable folios for 4KB base-page configs.

Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@localhost>
---
 arch/arm64/include/asm/pgtable.h |   1 +
 include/linux/fs.h               |   4 +-
 include/linux/pgtable.h          |  11 ++
 mm/filemap.c                     | 202 ++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 mm/internal.h                    |   4 +-
 mm/memory.c                      |  31 +++--
 mm/readahead.c                   |   9 +-
 7 files changed, 177 insertions(+), 85 deletions(-)

